cat-pstack is a fork of pstack-pro/pstack-workbuddy (commit aabc358). Port-specific files inherited from that fork (the port and validation scripts, hooks, install docs, the WorkBuddy harness notes, and CI) are Copyright (c) 2026 pstack-pro and are covered by the same MIT license.

Changes made in this fork, each documented in PORTING.md:

- Fixed conflicting `subagent_type` values in `skills/how`, `skills/interrogate`, and `skills/reflect`, caused by a blanket `readonly:` -> `subagent_type:` substitution.
- Restored the `automations/benny/` pack (12 files) that the upstream port dropped, adapted its paths, and added `automations/benny/WORKBUDDY.md` describing its real capability boundaries on WorkBuddy.
- Renamed the plugin to `cat-pstack`, so commands are `/cat-pstack:<skill>`.
- Fixed `scripts/validate.mjs` hard-coding the old plugin name, and added three regression guards for the defects above.
